WEBVTT

00:02.790 --> 00:11.030
We follow the birds, gaze at the stars, and measure the heavens to foretell the fates of our transient lives.

00:11.910 --> 00:17.470
You now guide the birds, stand among the stars, and move the heavens.

00:18.240 --> 00:27.160
As a spirit, forevermore shall your soul illuminate the sands upon which the very world is built.

00:27.840 --> 00:32.300
You will remain in the hearts of those
left behind on this castle-ship of mud.

00:49.080 --> 00:52.080
Become our guiding light.

00:53.790 --> 00:58.060
<i>93 Sand Era. Second day of the seventh month.</i>

00:58.780 --> 01:02.450
<i>A funeral was held for Benihi, one of the Marked.</i>

01:02.450 --> 01:06.640
<i>Age 29. She worked as an instructor.</i>

01:08.870 --> 01:12.620
<i>Our tradition is to drift the dead out into the sand ocean.</i>

01:13.380 --> 01:19.100
<i>Those who see the departed off are not allowed to shed tears.</i>

01:19.700 --> 01:25.520
<i>Any who do will be quickly taken in by
the countless souls sleeping beneath the sands.</i>

01:26.060 --> 01:28.900
<i>So our people believe.</i>

01:30.270 --> 01:32.280
Chakuro, you're not supposed to cry!

01:32.280 --> 01:35.320
Don't cry! The dead will beckon you down!

01:35.320 --> 01:36.420
Now, lace your fingers!

01:36.420 --> 01:38.620
Hold it in. Hold it in, Chakuro!

01:39.260 --> 01:40.730
Hold it in, hold it in!

01:43.900 --> 01:45.460
Dummy...

01:46.190 --> 01:48.080
I did it again.

01:48.620 --> 01:51.460
<i>I am Chakuro, a 14-year-old male.</i>

01:51.930 --> 01:54.260
<i>I serve as the archivist of the Mud Whale.</i>

01:55.120 --> 02:01.100
<i>Every time I see a dear friend off,
my urge to record grows stronger.</i>

02:03.420 --> 02:11.480
<i>My late Unmarked grandfather said I was inflicted with an illness that forced me to chronicle everything.</i>

02:13.070 --> 02:17.240
<i>Five hundred and thirteen people live on this drifting ship,</i>

02:17.240 --> 02:20.620
<i>sailing the boundless sand ocean on the Mud Whale.</i>

02:21.940 --> 02:28.840
<i>Our lives were bound to the sand, the wind, and the light of the sun.</i>

02:31.130 --> 02:34.050
Concentrate! Now let it down easy!

02:34.510 --> 02:37.200
Let it down easy...

02:37.800 --> 02:40.000
Yes, like that! Good work, everyone!

02:40.000 --> 02:42.570
Looks like the kids have improved a lot.

02:42.570 --> 02:43.260
Chakuro!

02:43.890 --> 02:45.720
I guess it's thanks to their great teacher.

02:45.720 --> 02:46.810
Guess so.

02:46.810 --> 02:48.810
They're all already better than you.

02:48.810 --> 02:49.770
That's harsh.

02:49.770 --> 02:53.550
The archivist usually isn't a Marked, you know?

02:53.550 --> 02:56.180
Thymia doesn't help with that job.

02:56.180 --> 03:00.320
So being appointed means you suck at using thymia, right?

03:00.320 --> 03:03.200
Forget sucking—they called me the "destroyer".

03:03.200 --> 03:04.660
Should <i>you</i> be laughing at that?

03:07.630 --> 03:14.810
Come to think of it, this was where Benihi taught us how to use our thymia too.

03:17.000 --> 03:20.620
Chakuro, let's just forget about Benihi.

03:20.620 --> 03:26.870
If we try to shoulder the burden of each person's death, we Marked won't be able to live in peace.

03:28.310 --> 03:29.640
You're right.

03:30.540 --> 03:35.360
<i>The "Marked" are those with the superhuman ability to control thymia with their emotions.</i>

03:35.360 --> 03:38.200
<i>Ninety percent of people on the Mud Whale are Marked.</i>

03:38.860 --> 03:43.560
<i>We Marked are short-lived,
like Benihi whom we sent off yesterday.</i>

03:43.560 --> 03:45.490
Chakuro!

03:45.490 --> 03:48.540
Cut us some leaves from those large sand bamboo!

03:48.540 --> 03:52.890
They're for food preservation, so grab five or six of the youngest ones you can from the top!

03:52.890 --> 03:53.480
What?

03:53.480 --> 03:54.910
Use this!

03:58.460 --> 04:00.690
<i>Five or six... five or six!</i>

04:11.090 --> 04:14.470
Chakuro! Who the hell said to chop the whole thing off?!

04:14.470 --> 04:16.270
Hey! Don't run, Chakuro!

04:16.270 --> 04:18.390
Get back here!

04:17.020 --> 04:18.390
What's all the noise?

04:18.390 --> 04:19.350
Who knows.

04:19.980 --> 04:21.330
Hide me!

04:21.330 --> 04:22.900
What'd you do this time?

04:22.900 --> 04:25.150
Uh, nothing really...

04:25.150 --> 04:26.630
Shut that before sand gets in.

04:26.630 --> 04:28.410
Oh, sorry!

04:28.410 --> 04:29.550
What's that?

04:29.550 --> 04:31.250
We're making goggles for you guys.

04:31.250 --> 04:32.160
For sand protection?

04:32.160 --> 04:34.410
Remember that acrylic plate we got?

04:34.410 --> 04:35.970
It's a prototype, but you can have it.

04:35.970 --> 04:36.880
Really?

04:36.880 --> 04:40.090
So cool! I love how hefty they are!

04:40.090 --> 04:43.950
We like elaborate designs in this workshop, but they're not functional.

04:43.950 --> 04:49.010
In exchange, next time you find something at sea or on an island, bring it right to us instead of turning it in.

04:50.260 --> 04:52.270
I can't wait to show these off to Sami.

04:53.120 --> 04:54.950
Oh, hello Chieftain.

04:54.950 --> 04:56.980
That's quite the stylish item you're wearing.

04:57.880 --> 04:59.170
Are you going to sea?

04:59.170 --> 05:02.070
No, I was just on my way to see Suou.

05:02.070 --> 05:04.280
Bringing your records, I suppose.

05:04.280 --> 05:08.580
Is that for Benihi's funeral service? It looks like you overdid it.

05:08.580 --> 05:12.090
Try to keep it in check.
Paper is a valuable resource.

05:12.090 --> 05:16.330
Oh, what's the harm?
Chakuro's records are incredibly helpful.

05:16.330 --> 05:20.160
Though they read more like diaries than official records.

05:20.160 --> 05:22.460
I just can't keep myself from writing.

05:22.460 --> 05:26.600
I don't think I'm suited to be an archivist.

05:26.600 --> 05:33.610
However, I find myself wishing that our predecessors of the Mud Whale had left more of their history.

05:33.610 --> 05:36.780
Like, why did they decide to live on this island?

05:36.780 --> 05:39.690
Or for instance, why doesn't the Mud Whale sink?

05:40.180 --> 05:45.490
If they had left more thorough records,
we might have answers to those questions.

05:45.490 --> 05:48.830
So I write for the future.

05:48.830 --> 05:49.870
Keep at it, then.

05:50.200 --> 05:50.990
I will.

05:51.740 --> 05:57.900
<i>The Chieftain and those on the Council of Elders are "Unmarked", and lack the ability to use thymia.</i>

05:58.830 --> 06:05.210
<i>Unlike the Marked who pass away in their twenties and thirties, the Unmarked are long-lived.</i>

06:05.890 --> 06:09.500
<i>They are the leaders of the Mud Whale.</i>

06:11.160 --> 06:11.920
Come in.

06:12.470 --> 06:14.020
Hello, Suou.

06:14.020 --> 06:15.450
Hey, Chakuro.

06:15.450 --> 06:17.120
I brought the records.

06:17.120 --> 06:18.210
Thank you.

06:20.500 --> 06:22.400
Were you crying all night?

06:22.400 --> 06:24.350
No, um...

06:25.890 --> 06:27.740
I was crying as well.

06:27.740 --> 06:29.720
Don't tell anyone else.

06:29.720 --> 06:31.540
Benihi was a good person.

06:34.410 --> 06:37.790
Your writing does not contain a hint of emotion.

06:38.450 --> 06:40.560
Even so, it is very touching.

06:40.560 --> 06:43.540
The rules say we aren't allowed to put our emotions into words.

06:44.140 --> 06:48.120
Chakuro, forgive me for making you write such painful records.

06:48.820 --> 06:50.560
I can't do anything myself.

06:50.560 --> 06:52.740
Wh-Why are you apologizing?

06:52.740 --> 06:56.690
You're doing research to figure out a way to extend the lifespans of the Marked!

06:56.690 --> 06:59.340
You grieve for our short lives more than anyone else!

06:59.340 --> 07:03.050
I know you've shed far more tears than I have.

07:03.050 --> 07:07.290
I'm not too bright, so all I can do is throw myself into my writing.

07:07.290 --> 07:10.440
But you're smart and long-lived!

07:10.440 --> 07:16.000
You can unravel the mysteries of the world and bring a greater happiness to the people of this ship!

07:16.730 --> 07:17.660
Thank you,

07:18.360 --> 07:19.230
Chakuro.

07:20.220 --> 07:25.640
<i>When the people here feel as though their emotions will show, they lace their fingers like this.</i>

07:26.320 --> 07:28.320
<i>They restrain their feelings.</i>

07:30.340 --> 07:37.050
<i>I hope that even after my death, these records will be of some use to you in the future.</i>

07:44.600 --> 07:46.190
It's a driftland!

07:46.870 --> 07:49.090
The first driftland in half a year has been spotted.

07:49.090 --> 07:53.040
We should be able to search it for supplies for roughly five days.

07:53.040 --> 07:56.310
After that it'll be dangerously far away.

07:56.310 --> 07:58.870
Prepare a scouting party to send tomorrow.

07:58.870 --> 08:02.080
If it proves to be safe, we will send a scavenging team.

08:02.450 --> 08:06.040
Please select people for the
scouting party by tomorrow, Suou.

08:06.040 --> 08:07.210
I leave it to you.

08:08.450 --> 08:09.930
Understood.

08:09.930 --> 08:14.870
<i>The next morning, we set sail while the waves were still calm.</i>

08:14.870 --> 08:18.970
Why's Chakuro gotta come too?
He better not make a mess of things.

08:19.640 --> 08:21.930
I'm surprised Suou included you, Sami.

08:21.930 --> 08:23.710
It may be dangerous.

08:23.710 --> 08:26.940
My brother has great faith in me!

08:26.940 --> 08:28.190
Let's go!

08:28.800 --> 08:34.450
<i>When traveling the sand ocean, thymia must be used to prevent the boats from sinking.</i>

08:34.850 --> 08:42.330
<i>The thymia used to float and propel the bamboo boats requires as much energy as a full-out sprint.</i>

08:42.330 --> 08:45.670
<i>As a result, our sailing range is limited.</i>

08:45.670 --> 08:47.770
Listen up! No going solo!

08:47.770 --> 08:51.050
Also, we're only here to scout,
so don't take anything back with you.

08:51.050 --> 08:52.510
Okay.

08:54.180 --> 08:55.070
Sami.

08:56.680 --> 08:57.600
Thanks.

08:57.600 --> 08:58.350
Sure.

08:59.520 --> 09:00.640
How romantic!

09:00.640 --> 09:01.970
We're not like that!

09:02.310 --> 09:05.190
Wait, Sami! He said not to go alone!

09:05.190 --> 09:06.200
It's fine.

09:07.020 --> 09:12.060
Still, this looks pretty different from the usual drifting islands.

09:16.780 --> 09:18.710
A human tool!

09:18.710 --> 09:20.490
It looks like a weapon.

09:20.490 --> 09:24.960
<i>There have been several islands with tools left by past civilizations before.</i>

09:24.960 --> 09:27.810
<i>Despite that, we've never seen a single soul.</i>

09:27.810 --> 09:29.540
The workshop guys are going to love this.

09:29.870 --> 09:30.900
Right, Sami?

09:30.900 --> 09:31.630
Huh?

09:32.450 --> 09:33.050
Sami?

09:34.000 --> 09:35.330
Oh no...

09:35.330 --> 09:37.220
Hey, Sami!

09:41.760 --> 09:43.020
What are you?

09:49.260 --> 09:50.390
Hey!

09:55.530 --> 09:57.570
Wait! Get back here!

09:59.820 --> 10:01.160
What's this?

10:01.920 --> 10:03.080
Food?

10:33.970 --> 10:34.830
Um...

10:40.200 --> 10:41.330
Are you okay?

10:45.450 --> 10:46.960
<i>Tears.</i>

10:46.960 --> 10:49.070
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

10:58.690 --> 11:04.850
<i>She was the first human I ever met outside those on the Mud Whale.</i>

11:05.650 --> 11:10.810
<i>That is, if her condition at that moment could even be considered "human".</i>

11:11.460 --> 11:12.470
<i>However...</i>

11:20.000 --> 11:21.530
Stop!

11:27.700 --> 11:30.160
<i>Her power weakened.</i>

11:37.520 --> 11:39.980
As I thought... she's hurt.

11:46.130 --> 11:48.010
Was she washing these?

11:59.480 --> 12:02.730
H-Hey, you're coming too?

12:02.730 --> 12:04.870
Are you her pet?

12:06.290 --> 12:07.080
Huh?

12:07.080 --> 12:08.730
Where's Chakuro?

12:08.730 --> 12:10.680
We got split up along the way.

12:10.680 --> 12:11.950
Masoo!

12:12.790 --> 12:16.010
Hey, Chakuro! I told you not to go it alone!

12:16.010 --> 12:18.040
You even picked something up!

12:17.290 --> 12:18.960
No, she's not a thing.

12:18.960 --> 12:20.210
She's a person! A person!

12:22.760 --> 12:23.880
S-Seriously?

12:24.970 --> 12:26.290
What should we do, Captain?

12:26.290 --> 12:28.830
She's really weak! She might even die if we leave her!

12:30.410 --> 12:37.780
<i>We withdrew from our scouting mission immediately, and decided to bring her back to the Mud Whale.</i>

12:39.400 --> 12:41.200
She's pretty.

12:41.200 --> 12:44.990
Sami, could you put these clothes on her? I think they're hers.

12:44.990 --> 12:45.660
Sure.

12:48.560 --> 12:52.200
This looks like a really old scar.

12:53.220 --> 12:58.310
<i>I should probably keep her attacking me with thymia to myself.</i>

13:01.130 --> 13:01.880
It's rain.

13:02.820 --> 13:03.840
But the sun's out!

13:03.840 --> 13:05.380
It feels great!

13:06.410 --> 13:13.070
<i>Rain is an indispensable part of our livelihood on the Mud Whale, as it helps to fill up our reservoirs.</i>

13:13.700 --> 13:16.760
<i>It is said that rainy weather is a good omen.</i>

13:17.440 --> 13:18.810
Even a rainbow!

13:18.810 --> 13:20.330
Good luck is on the horizon.

13:20.330 --> 13:21.470
Yeah!

13:21.470 --> 13:29.890
<i>This girl may take us from our small,
enclosed world to a future nobody could have foreseen.</i>

13:30.530 --> 13:33.610
<i>The scouting party returned with a spring in their step.</i>

13:33.610 --> 13:37.520
<i>In particular, as I was the one who found her first—</i>

13:38.190 --> 13:39.960
<i>Right, I can't write emotionally.</i>

13:39.960 --> 13:42.190
What's wrong? You're back early.

13:42.190 --> 13:44.940
It's an emergency. We brought back something you won't believe.

13:44.940 --> 13:46.170
What was that?

13:46.170 --> 13:49.750
Didn't I tell you it was forbidden to bring anything back today?

13:49.750 --> 13:51.430
The Council of Elders will be notified.

13:51.430 --> 13:53.930
Huh?! Shut up, you bonehead!

13:53.930 --> 13:56.520
Wanna say that again, you musclehead?!

13:56.950 --> 13:58.890
Stop that at once, you two.

13:58.890 --> 14:02.020
Let's lace our fingers, unless you'd rather be sent to the bowels!

14:02.020 --> 14:04.720
Why don't you take a look already, dumbass!

14:04.720 --> 14:06.750
We found a person on the island!

14:06.750 --> 14:07.620
A person?

14:07.620 --> 14:08.530
She's here.

14:09.850 --> 14:12.160
A p-person?!

14:12.160 --> 14:15.390
L-Lady Taisha!

14:17.760 --> 14:18.720
She's awake.

14:27.710 --> 14:28.680
An aura?

14:28.680 --> 14:29.600
You wanna go?!

14:29.600 --> 14:31.760
Stop that! You mustn't fight with thymia!

14:31.760 --> 14:35.210
If you do something like that on the Mud Whale, you'll be punished.

14:37.250 --> 14:38.230
Let go.

14:38.230 --> 14:39.460
She spoke!

14:39.460 --> 14:40.600
In our language...

14:42.720 --> 14:46.480
I see I've been taken captive.

14:48.280 --> 14:52.500
I won't resist. I'm the only one left.

14:53.270 --> 14:55.830
I... surrender.

14:58.800 --> 15:01.700
She's this way. Please watch your step.

15:01.700 --> 15:02.630
Thank you.

15:02.630 --> 15:03.880
Oh no, it's nothing!

15:04.320 --> 15:06.320
Where is the island girl?

15:07.050 --> 15:11.070
She was just taken to the infirmary by Chakuro and Sami.

15:11.850 --> 15:15.490
Those damn brats!

15:15.490 --> 15:17.100
What's your name?

15:18.280 --> 15:19.440
I lack that.

15:19.440 --> 15:24.030
What do you mean? I saw "Lykos" embroidered into your clothes.

15:24.030 --> 15:25.110
Lykos, huh.

15:25.490 --> 15:28.670
Lykos, you're not surprised to suddenly be somewhere unknown?

15:28.670 --> 15:30.770
My heart would be pounding out of my chest.

15:30.770 --> 15:33.030
I'd be super curious!

15:33.700 --> 15:34.780
I lack that.

15:38.280 --> 15:40.210
This is the infirmary?

15:41.170 --> 15:42.860
It's full of young people.

15:42.860 --> 15:44.290
They're all Marked.

15:45.090 --> 15:49.860
Around when we turn thirty, both our thymia and physical strength start to deteriorate.

15:49.860 --> 15:51.850
Some become bedridden.

15:52.380 --> 15:54.170
Is it like that where you're from?

15:56.010 --> 15:57.390
We lack that.

15:57.790 --> 16:00.330
Is this... Falena?

16:00.330 --> 16:04.690
Falena? This is the Mud Whale. We all call it that.

16:04.690 --> 16:06.360
Chakuro, Sami.

16:06.360 --> 16:07.630
Chieftain.

16:07.630 --> 16:10.820
Were you looking after the girl? Well done.

16:12.070 --> 16:15.130
Hello. I'm the Chieftain, Taisha.

16:15.130 --> 16:17.050
Would you mind coming with me?

16:17.050 --> 16:19.770
Hold on, Chieftain.
Where are you taking her?

16:19.770 --> 16:21.760
To be introduced to the Council of Elders.

16:21.760 --> 16:24.660
But we need to have someone look over her injuries first.

16:24.660 --> 16:26.990
You two are so kind.

16:26.990 --> 16:30.090
But you needn't worry.
We'll take good care of her.

16:30.090 --> 16:32.680
Please deal with the bowel moles, Suou.

16:32.680 --> 16:33.430
Yes.

16:36.370 --> 16:37.510
Lykos...

16:39.720 --> 16:40.520
Big brother!

16:40.910 --> 16:44.260
Did you see? She's the girl we found on the island.

16:44.260 --> 16:46.650
Do you think she'll be my friend?

16:46.650 --> 16:48.880
Yes, I'm sure she will be.

16:48.880 --> 16:49.660
Yeah!

16:49.660 --> 16:52.820
Suou, what's happening with the bowel moles?

16:52.820 --> 16:55.660
A rainbow appeared, so they're being pardoned.

16:55.660 --> 16:56.780
Ouni and his gang are?

16:58.690 --> 17:01.690
I'm about to go release them.

17:02.200 --> 17:06.790
But who knows what they'll do once they hear someone's been found on a driftland...

17:07.120 --> 17:09.640
I'll come with you! As your bodyguard!

17:09.640 --> 17:10.680
I'll go too!

17:10.680 --> 17:12.660
No! You go back to work, Sami.

17:12.660 --> 17:13.760
C'mon!

17:16.840 --> 17:19.160
Did you pick that up from the island too?

17:19.160 --> 17:19.810
Huh?

17:19.810 --> 17:21.920
Oh, he joined on his own.

17:21.920 --> 17:22.950
Looks delicious.

17:22.950 --> 17:24.920
Er, right...

17:24.920 --> 17:32.000
<i>On the Mud Whale, those who break the laws are
imprisoned in an underground space known as the "bowels".</i>

17:32.000 --> 17:35.250
<i>For some reason, thymia cannot be used here.</i>

17:35.830 --> 17:42.450
<i>It was a harsh punishment indeed for the short-lived Marked to have their freedom restricted in the bowels.</i>

17:42.450 --> 17:48.130
<i>Even so, there were some repeat offenders who were sent there time and time again.</i>

17:48.570 --> 17:54.460
<i>Due to their extended time in the bowels, they came to be known as "bowel moles".</i>

17:54.460 --> 17:56.970
You've been pardoned. Get out.

17:58.050 --> 17:59.430
My back hurts!

17:59.430 --> 18:00.700
It's so bright!

18:00.700 --> 18:03.560
What an honor to be met by the future Chieftain.

18:04.690 --> 18:07.370
Please refrain from repeating your foolish actions.

18:07.370 --> 18:09.900
You must treasure your limited time.

18:09.900 --> 18:11.110
Treasure it?

18:11.110 --> 18:14.300
It's the same whether we're
under the ground or above it.

18:14.300 --> 18:17.610
In a world this small, it doesn't matter what we do.

18:17.610 --> 18:22.330
You long-lived Unmarked can treasure your lives on this mud boat all you want.

18:22.950 --> 18:28.170
You should be aware that a person was found on a driftland today.

18:28.170 --> 18:29.370
Hey, is that true?

18:29.370 --> 18:31.160
They found a person? <i>Outside</i>?

18:31.160 --> 18:33.590
Please try not to overreact.

18:33.590 --> 18:35.410
As it stands, you already—

18:34.560 --> 18:36.660
I knew there was a world outside!

18:36.660 --> 18:38.330
A world where other people live!

18:38.330 --> 18:39.180
We can't say for—

18:41.140 --> 18:43.160
We're leaving.

18:43.160 --> 18:48.350
If a different world exists outside,
we're abandoning this tiny little ship.

18:48.350 --> 18:49.560
Ouni!

18:49.560 --> 18:51.940
Hey! Where's that person?

18:51.940 --> 18:52.580
I will not say.

18:52.580 --> 18:53.980
Don't rely on him.

18:55.450 --> 18:56.940
Wait, Ouni!

18:56.940 --> 18:58.350
Ouni!

18:58.350 --> 19:05.300
<i>Ouni was the leader of the bowel moles, and it was said he had the greatest thymia ability on the Mud Whale.</i>

19:06.190 --> 19:09.210
Honestly... this is exactly what I feared.

19:09.210 --> 19:11.630
They might try to do something to Lykos.

19:11.630 --> 19:12.880
I'm going!

19:12.880 --> 19:13.910
Chakuro!

19:25.140 --> 19:26.970
<i>Lykos...</i>

19:26.970 --> 19:30.130
<i>It's only Lykos and the Elders in there?</i>

19:30.130 --> 19:32.780
What is the name of your country?

19:32.780 --> 19:36.540
Were you dispatched from the Mainland?

19:36.540 --> 19:38.690
<i>Mainland? What are they talking about?</i>

19:38.690 --> 19:42.020
Please answer my question first.

19:43.110 --> 19:45.280
Is this Falena?

19:45.280 --> 19:47.020
We cannot answer that.

19:47.020 --> 19:53.000
As long as we remain unsure of your goals, we are unable to reveal who we are.

19:53.000 --> 19:57.210
<i>What does that mean? Do the Elders understand what Lykos is asking?</i>

19:58.100 --> 20:02.570
I was brought here against my will.

20:02.570 --> 20:04.420
Have you allies on the island?

20:05.090 --> 20:06.680
They all died.

20:07.020 --> 20:08.970
I buried them.

20:08.970 --> 20:12.100
Did doing so not cause you to suffer any painful feelings?

20:13.450 --> 20:14.480
I lack that.

20:14.480 --> 20:16.270
She's an Apathoia...

20:16.270 --> 20:18.010
A person without emotions.

20:18.010 --> 20:19.570
How can this be...

20:19.570 --> 20:21.570
<i>Apathoia? What's that?</i>

20:21.570 --> 20:25.730
As we feared, the world has yet to change.

20:25.730 --> 20:28.910
It appears there is no point in continuing our conversation.

20:28.910 --> 20:32.210
Forgive us, but we must restrain you.

20:32.210 --> 20:32.980
Lykos!

20:34.170 --> 20:35.470
What are you doing?

20:35.470 --> 20:37.630
He says to watch out above you.

20:44.190 --> 20:45.680
Ouni!

20:45.680 --> 20:49.390
Stop at once! Do you understand what will become of you after this?

20:50.270 --> 20:52.430
I'm going to go see her world.

20:52.770 --> 20:55.730
The rest of you can spend your entire lives playing mud boat here!

20:55.730 --> 20:56.350
Lykos—

21:04.880 --> 21:06.950
Someone... anyone...

21:06.950 --> 21:08.070
What happened?!

21:08.070 --> 21:12.500
They mustn't... If they contact
the world, calamity will befall us!

21:13.840 --> 21:16.390
Ouni kidnapped the island girl and ran!

21:16.390 --> 21:18.080
Hurry up and catch him!

21:18.080 --> 21:20.000
Ouni, what are you planning?!

21:20.000 --> 21:21.210
I'm going to her island.

21:21.210 --> 21:22.310
What?

21:22.310 --> 21:25.180
You were part of the scouting party, right?

21:25.180 --> 21:25.930
Yeah...

21:25.930 --> 21:26.930
Lead me there.

21:30.660 --> 21:35.560
<i>There is much I want to write about the Mud Whale.</i>

21:36.310 --> 21:42.360
<i>In those toy-like castle towers built of countless sun-dried bricks of mud,</i>

21:42.360 --> 21:46.520
<i>many people could only live their lives reliant on them.</i>

21:47.370 --> 21:52.700
<i>Much happened that would surprise those of you who live in a boundless world.</i>

21:54.430 --> 21:58.840
<i>This island was the entirety of our precious world.</i>

22:00.170 --> 22:02.840
<i>No matter what may become of me,</i>

22:03.150 --> 22:05.840
<i>I want to continue writing</i>

22:07.280 --> 22:09.850
<i>about everything that happened to us.</i>
